  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-quote-reply",
      "text": "Quote & reply for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness), the way Claude Code does it.\n\n[中文](README.zh.md) · MIT\n\nSelect text → answer it in a popover → the pair becomes a block above the composer → send them all at once."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Selection pill, reply popover, `Enter` to add.\n- 76×76 blocks: two quote lines with a rule, two lines of your answer.\n- Composer text stays yours; it lands last in the message.\n- Images in the draft travel with the message.\n- Real quote rules in the transcript, not `│` characters.\n- Chinese and English, following the app language."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-quote-reply)\n\nRequires DSH 0.2.x with the desktop/web conversation UI.\n\n- **npm** → `dsh plugin add dsh-quote-reply`\n- **Plugin Manager** → *Add plugin* → this directory.\n- **Git** → `plugin_manager install_bundle target: git+https://github.com/gf691271/dsh-quote-reply#<commit>`\n- **Market index** → add `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gf691271/dsh-quote-reply/main/market/index.json`"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. Select text in any message.\n2. Click `Quote Text`, write your answer, press `Enter`.\n3. Repeat, then press `Enter` in the composer (or click **Send**)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- `│` at the start of a line is the storage marker; the transcript renders it as a rule.\n- A send the host refuses keeps your blocks and text; nothing is lost.\n- File attachments (PDF, zip) cannot ride a quote and stop the send with a notice."
    }
  ],
